    "cwe_ids": [],
    "description": "### Impact\r\nA vulnerability exists in the User API Key device authorization flow in Discourse. An authenticated user with permission to create user API keys (by default, this includes Trust Level 0 users on sites with open registration) could exploit a parameter handling flaw to authorize a device key for a different user account. The resulting key grants the attacker the same access and privileges as the victim, leading to potential data exposure and unauthorized actions within the application.\r\n\r\n### Workarounds\r\nNo known workarounds for this issue\n\nDiscovered by Anthropic's OSS Scanner, as vulnerability ANT-2026-2RCWW0D2.",
